lan-chat (0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Connectionless UDP design: one JSON datagram per event on
    port 5055, no server, no handshakes, no message framing
  * Survives lossy WiFi: heartbeats and messages are sent as
    subnet-directed broadcast plus unicast to every known peer,
    and sequence numbers make the duplicates invisible, so
    neither peers nor messages get lost
  * Presence lifecycle: peers are dimmed after 8 s without a
    heartbeat and removed after 60 s, so vanished peers
    disappear cleanly
  * Several instances coexist: random instance ids, the same
    user on multiple PCs shows up as name@machine, and private
    notes still reach the right instance
  * Copy and paste first: click a message to copy its bare text
    (no timestamp, no sender), triple-click selects the whole
    received message, drag text or a small text file onto the
    window to compose, drag a user to send a private note
  * debian packaging with the help of equivs

 -- Martin Homuth-Rosemann <Ho-Ro@github.com>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:18:15 +0200
